{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Closure Property.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Closure Property.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"closure property closure property","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Closure Property.md","fileName":"Closure Property.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Closure Property","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 23:41\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Number Systems and Arithmetic]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Number Systems and Arithmetic","Integer","Rational Number","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Closure Property.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Closure Property.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"closure property closure property","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Closure Property.md","fileName":"Closure Property.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Closure Property","heading":"Closure Property","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A collection is closed under an operation when applying that operation to any allowed inputs always produces another member of the same collection. For natural numbers (a) and (b), both (a+b) and (ab) are natural numbers, so (mathbb{N}) is closed under addition and multiplication.\n\nClosure depends on both the operation and the number system. Natural numbers are not closed under subtraction or division, because results such as (3-5) and (3/5) leave the set. [[Integer]]s repair closure under subtraction, while [[Rational Number]]s also accommodate division by nonzero values.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Number Systems and Arithmetic","Integer","Rational Number","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Closure Property.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Closure Property.md","sourceType":"markdown",